cff-version: 1.1.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article below."
title: "MLmrpi: Machine Learning Multi-Response Performance Index"
abstract: >-
  Python package to rank machine-learning models from their precomputed
  performance metrics (R2, MSE, RMSE, MAE, ...) with a single composite index,
  the MLmrpi, computed by five multi-response methods: Assignment of Weights
  (AW), Data Envelopment Analysis-based Ranking (DEAR), Grey Relational
  Analysis (GRA), Factor Analysis (FA) and Multi-Response Normalized Value
  (MRNV). It also provides the agreement and robustness analyses of the
  associated article (Cohen's kappa, Fleiss' kappa, Kendall's W, correlations,
  performance tiers, Shapiro-Wilk and Wilcoxon tests).
